Rackmount and Cabinet AlphaServer 1000 4/266 Systems

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Offers leadership price/performance, expandability, and multiple
   in-cabinet system integration

o  High performance for PC LAN, Internet access, and clustering

o  Industry standard PCI/EISA options; seven EISA slots, two PCI slots, and
   one combo PCI/EISA slot for maximum configuration flexibility

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The AlphaServer 1000 4/266 Rackmount system is the 266 MHz Alpha
uniprocessor server follow-on to the 233 MHz system, configured into a
rackmount tower enclosure. While functionally similar, the rackmount
tower has a different chassis layout from the deskside system enclosure.

Like the AlphaServer 1000 4/200 and 4/233 systems, it will run Digital
UNIX, OpenVMS, and Windows NT. It shares with those systems such
reliability features as ECC memory, ECC cache, RAID configurations, hot
swap StorageWorks disks, and availability as a custom Internet system.

The AlphaServer 1000 4/266 Rackmount system supports

o  PCI-based FDDI RAID controller
o  Asynchronous multiplexer
o  Remote diagnosis
o  Up to 1 GB of RAM
o  Wide SCSI devices (require wide controller)
o  Dual SCSI backplane
o  DEC safe Available Server for Digital UNIX and OpenVMS SCSI clusters

The following components are integrated on the system motherboard:

o  Industry standard SVGA controller
o  Floppy disk controller
o  Two serial ports; one parallel port
o  Keyboard and mouse controller
o  LCD operator control panel
o  PCI-based fast SCSI-2 controller

Six mass storage devices are also supported, including a floppy diskette
and CD-ROM. Internal disk storage supports up to 12.9 GB using three 4.3
GB disk drives. Rackmounted StorageWorks shelving allows additional disk
storage, and field installed CPU upgrades are available.

The AlphaServer 1000 4/266 rackmount systems are available as System
Building Blocks and as preconfigured packages, containing

o  One H9A10 19-inch wide ANSI/EIA rackmount cabinet
o  One Rackmount StorageWorks shelf with one disk drive
o  A UPS system (optional)

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

Rackmount and cabinet systems are available now. System Building Blocks
require memory, disks, CD-ROM, monitor, power cord, and cabinet enclosure
(if appropriate). Packaged systems require cabinet enclosure and monitor
(if appropriate).

