PCI-Token Ring Network Adapter

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Supports speeds of either 4 or 16 megabits per second under software
   control

o  Offers Plug and Play auto configuration

o  Full software driver support for the Windows NT, Digital UNIX, and
   OpenVMS operating systems

o  Supports 100 Ohm unshielded twisted pair (UTP) or 150 Ohm shielded
   twisted pair (STP) cabling

o  Compliant with FCC Class B and CEmark standards

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The PCI-Token Ring network adapter (PBXNP-AA) is a high performance 16
megabits per second (Mb/s) or 4 megabits per second (Mb/s) token ring
adapter that utilizes bus master data transfer over a 32 bit PCI bus.
Fully compliant with PCI local bus specification V2.0, the PCI-Token Ring
adapter uses bus mastering technology to maximize throughput and minimize
CPU utilization. The PCI-Token Ring adapter also complies with the IEEE
802.2 Media Access Control (MAC), Logical Link Control (LLC), and IEEE
802.5 Media Access Control (MAC) Token Ring standards.

The PCI-Token Ring network adapter offers support for Windows NT,
OpenVMS, and Digital UNIX physical layer software drivers. The Windows NT
software driver, which is compatible with the Windows NT 3.51 operating
system, is available now. The OpenVMS software driver, which runs on
OpenVMS V6.2, is shipped with the adapter. OpenVMS support will be
included in the next functional release. The Digital UNIX software driver
will be available with future revisions of Digital UNIX V3.2. The UNIX
software driver will also be supported in hardware release V3.2E and in
Digital UNIX V4.0 in the beginning of 1996.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The PCI-Token Ring adapter can be ordered now for delivery on November 1,
1995, from Digital and its business partners. The PCI-Token Ring adapter
comes with a five year warranty.

Order No.           Description

PBXNP-AA            PCI-Token Ring Adapter

TECHNICAL DATA

o  The PCI-Token Ring adapter connects to 16 or 4 Mb/s Token Ring networks
   using either category 3, 4, or 5 100 ohm UTP (unshielded twisted pair) or
   a DB9 connector for Type 1 150 ohm STP (shielded twisted pair) cabling.

o  The PCI-Token Ring adapter supports Plug and Play auto configuration by
   connecting to the Token Ring network via an IEEE 802.5 compliant Token
   Ring wiring concentrator called MAU.

o  DECnet/OSI for Digital UNIX and DECnet/OSI for OpenVMS software layered
   product support will be available with the products' next software
   releases.

o  SNA Peer server for Digital UNIX software layered product support will be
   available with the next SNA peer server release.

o  The maximum throughput for the PCI-Token Ring adapter is a factor of the
   protocol stacks, packet sizes, I/O bus loading, and relative CPU power.
   At the data link/driver level, this equates to data rates in excess of
   15.8 Mb/s when the 16 Mb/s speed is selected.

o  The PCI-Token Ring adapter is compliant with FCC Class B,
   CEmark-EN55022/EN50082-1 Class B, VCCI level 2, UL 1950, CSA, and
   TUV-EN60950 standards.

