Digital Reselling WebServer products for Digital UNIX

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Agreement includes four products: WebServer, Secure WebServer, Security
   Module, and WebReporter

o  Secure HTTP and SSL allow for the broadest possible access in secure
   environments

o  WebReporter analyzes Web server access activity; generates customized
   reports

o  Initial release on Digital UNIX platform; OpenVMS Alpha, Windows NT
   Alpha, and Intel NT soon to follow

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Digital's reseller agreement with Open Market Inc., makes available four
products for Digital UNIX users: WebServer, Secure WebServer, Security
Module, and WebReporter.

WebServer

The Open Market WebServer V1.1 is an advanced software product designed
to meet the challenges of companies demanding thousands of simultaneous
connections in mission-critical production environments. The Open Market
WebServer sets the standard for performance and functionality while
providing unrivaled interoperability with every (World Wide Web) browser.

The Open Market WebServer offers the following features:

o  Multi-threaded architecture that supports over 1,000 concurrent client
   connections

o  Designed according to Web standards

   - Common Gateway Interface (CGI/1.1), the standard interface for server
     scripts
   - HyperText Transport Protocol (HTTP/1.0), for interoperability with all
     existing Web clients
   - Support for a variety of file types, including Java, GIF, JPEG, and
     MPEG
   - VRML and HTML V3

o  Incorporates a powerful access control scripting language for
   implementing complex access policies--WebServer administrators can
   control access based on host, time of day, user name, browser software
   type, authentication method, and other parameters

o  Enhanced logging

   - Integrated format, all access, error, and security information is
     recorded in a single record
   - Additional information fields, such as browser software type, referring
     URL, security information, and request begin/end times
   - Named field format that is designed for easy parsing and future
     expansion

o  Supports the "common" log format, for compatibility with existing log
   analysis and reporting tools

   - WebReporter software analyzes extended format logs and generates
     customized reports of server activity

o  Built-in support for clickable images (image maps)

o  Directory indexing

o  Simple, forms-based installation

Secure WebServer

The Open Market Secure WebServer includes all of the features of the Open
Market WebServer plus security capabilities. Secure WebServerV1.1 is the
first WWW server to support both Secure HyperText Transfer Protocol
(Secure HTTP) and the Secure Sockets Layer (SSL). The combination of
Secure HTTP and SSL allows for the broadest possible access in secure
environments.

S-HTTP, the emerging standard for secure communication on the Web, is
superior in its ability to

o  Authenticate clients
o  Fully authenticate servers (including checks of revocation lists and
   support for certificate chaining or hierarchies)
o  Support digital signatures (attesting to message authenticity)
o  Negotiate security levels based on application needs
o  Provide secure communication through existing corporate firewalls

The SSL protocol provides

o  Privacy between client and server
o  Server authentication
o  Reliable communications between client and server

A Security Module upgrades the WebServer to the Secure WebServer. Two
versions of this module are available

o  Security Module (U.S. and Canada) -- Available for purchase by users in
   the U.S. and Canada
o  Security Module (Global) -- Approved for purchase by users outside the
   U.S. and Canada

WebReporter

WebReporter is a sophisticated tool for analyzing Web server access
activity and generating customized reports. WebReporter supports the Open
Market WebServer's Extended Log Format, as well as the common log format
used by other Web servers. WebReporter uses a powerful scripting language
for controlling report data and format. The scripting language allows the
user to

o  Assign names to groups of URLs and host names
o  Specify filters to select or omit log entries
o  Include previously processed log data into new reports (eliminates the
   need to process the entire log file each time there are new entries)
o  Generate plain text or HTML-format reports from multiple log formats, in
   either uncompressed or compressed files
o  Generate reports prepared for import into spreadsheets
o  Convert from one log file format to another
o  Create log file subsets for management of very large log files

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The WebServer, Secure WebServer, Security Module, and WebReporter
products are available now from Digital.

