PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The Digital SNA APPC/LU6.2 Programming Interface V3.0 for Digital UNIX
supports the development and running of cross platform applications
between Digital UNIX and IBM mainframe and AS/400 systems in an IBM SNA
environment. This product is based on LU6.2 technology, which was
developed for and used in the CICS for Digital UNIX product.

The Digital SNA APPC/LU6.2 Programming Interface V3.0 for Digital UNIX
supports TCP/IP and DECnet environments through the use of Digital SNA
Gateways. TCP/IP or DECnet connections are supported by the DEC SNA Peer
Server or DEC SNA Domain Gateway. For DECnet only connections, the DEC
SNA Gateway for Synchronous Transport and DEC SNA Gateway for Channel
Transport are used.

Features of the Digital SNA APPC/LU6.2 Programming Interface V3.0 for
Digital UNIX include

o  CPI-C interface adherence to the IBM CPI-C V1.1 and V1.2 specifications,
   with the exception of non-blocking calls

o  Support for basic and mapped LU6.2 conversation verbs, which provides
   flexibility in application development

o  Capability for parallel sessions, which ensures efficient usage of system
   resources

o  Support for synchronous and thread re-entrant usage

