Purveyor WebServer V1.1 for Windows NT

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Process Software's Purveyor WebServer V1.1 for Windows NT is a powerful,
second generation product that allows users to manage their presence on
the World Wide Web. A number of features in this release, such as a Proxy
Server, WAIS Search Engine, ODBC, SQL support, error logging, customized
report generation remote administration capability, and Visual Basic,all
help users build secure, high performance web sites. These features can
reduce costs and support requirements.

Purveyor's Access Control security features let users share or restrict
access to a file or directory by either using a domain name or an IP
address. Purveyor allows the use of wildcards throughout its access
control configuration, which gives the web site administrator unlimited
control and flexibility.

Designed as a true Windows NT application, Purveyor is based on EMWAC Web
Server technology funded by Microsoft and Digital. The graphical user
interface and point-and-click commands provide users with a Windows "look
and feel." Purveyor has added "Cool Tools" freeware to the kit.  This
disk supplies a set of shareware for Purveyor's web server and other
Internet utilities.

BENEFITS

o  Virtual Servers/Multiple Site Hosting based on IP address -- Allows
   Internet information providers to support and manage multiple home pages.
   Each Virtual Server has its own access control, data directory, and
   traffic and logging information, and each can be configured and addressed
   via its unique IP address or domain.

o  Detailed product information -- By integrating the information contained
   on corporate databases with web servers, users who access the site can
   receive detailed information from the site's hosting organization.
   Purveyor V1.1 supports Microsoft's ODBC and SQL Server.

o  High-performance application programming interface alternative to the
   Common Gateway Interface (CGI) -- Allows developers to integrate Web
   technology with new and existing back-end applications.

o  Enhanced log viewer program -- GUI-based point-and-click application that
   allows customization and management of information captured in the
   Purveyor Log Files. This information can be imported into Microsoft Excel
   spreadsheets.

o  Search engine support -- Product software supports local text searches of
   the Web for easy access to targeted information. Using WAIS technology,
   the HTML output provides hypertext links to the materials that satisfy
   the specifications of the search query.

o  Link browser -- This application allows users to create a "visual map" of
   the links between local and remote HTML documents, finds "broken" links
   on the server, starts an editing program to fix problems, and saves
   snapshots of the system.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

