Multia Enterprise Client with Pentium Processor

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Expands the Multia enterprise client to Intel platforms

o  Built-in configuration management for lowest desktop administration costs

o  Delivers simultaneous access to UNIX operating system, PC, and legacy
   applications

o  Embedded industry-standard network protocols

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The Multia Enterprise Client is the solution for users who need to
integrate PC, UNIX, OpenVMS, and legacy applications into a single,
centrally managed desktop. Using industry-standard network protocols, the
Multia Enterprise Client systems can access applications and data
anywhere on the network.

Multia Enterprise Client expands the current Alpha-based Multia family
with high-performance Intel Pentium 100-MHz models. Multia is a fully
integrated hardware/software desktop that enables users to simultaneously
run Windows NT, Windows 95, and Windows applications locally, while
accessing UNIX and OpenVMS applications via an integrated X server.
Terminal-based applications are accessed through embedded emulators. The
Multia Enterprise Client software is designed using industry-standard
technology with value-added features, such as Configuration Manager,
which allows system administrators to centrally manage each Multia
desktop on the network. Its PCI-based hardware design provides integrated
Ethernet, graphics, and audio capability in a very small footprint.

Multia is a lower cost platform than PC's because it includes many
features and options as part of its standard configuration, including
Configuration and Application Managers; Kea! VT340/420 Terminal
Emulation; embedded network protocols, such as DECnet, LAT, and NFS (with
X server option); built-in Ethernet support; and built-in graphics and
audio capabilities.

Each Multia Enterprise Client model comes with pre-installed software, so
no lengthy installations are required. Multia workgroups can be
preconfigured by the system administrator so that each Multia user is
automatically configured for application access at power up. One Multia
System Administrator Kit must be purchased for each installation. Multia
software options include the Multia X Server Option V3.1 and RUMBA for
Mainframe for Multia Option V3.1.

Multia Base Software V3.1 for Intel

Multia Base Software is factory installed on each Multia Enterprise
Client model. Features include

o  Multia Configuration Manager -- Lets system administrators remotely
   manage and configure Multia desktops on the network.  It can be used to
   create workgroups of users with common application requirements and skill
   sets. Workgroup definitions can include access to networked applications;
   availability of hardware options; and settings for keyboard, desktop,
   network, and software options. System administrators can lock or unlock
   any Multia feature. The Configuration Manager supports both LAN and WAN
   environments and provides password protection. The status feature enables
   a system administrator to query any Multia system in the environment to
   obtain information on network counters, which applications are being
   accessed, and system configuration data. Multia Configuration Manager is
   complementary to management software, such as SMS and AssetWORKS. The
   Multia Enterprise Client can be managed by SMS and AssetWORKS management
   software in the same way as any other Windows NT device. The Multia
   Configuration Manager is used to control and customize Multia desktop
   attributes.

o  Multia Application Manager -- This is the user's primary interface to the
   Multia client and is used for accessing local and remote applications.
   Application icons are displayed in a customizable control panel. The list
   of available applications, their location on the network, the transport
   used to access them, and their startup procedures are all predefined
   remotely by the system administrator. End users simply point and click on
   an icon to startup an application session. The autostart option is used
   to select which applications startup automatically at the beginning of a
   Multia session.

o  Windows NT Workstation 3.51 operating system --Microsoft's powerful,
   advanced 32-bit, multitasking operating system provides the power of a
   workstation with the ease of use, productivity, and compatibility of a
   personal computer. It includes integrated networking (TCP/IP, NETBEUI,
   and IPX/SPX) and is compatible with Windows, MS-DOS, OS/2, and POSIX
   applications.

o  Embedded network protocols -- DECnet and LAT (32-sessions, Service
   Classes 1, 3, and 4) are included, in addition to the protocols available
   with Windows NT Workstation 3.51.

o  Kea! VT340/420 terminal emulation -- This local terminal emulator
   provides full VT340 graphics, VT420 text, and Tektronics 4010/4014
   terminal emulation.

o  Reference Desk -- Provides users with online information about Multia,
   including a graphical user tutorial; problem solving; context-sensitive
   help; system administrator's information and online help; and information
   on software and hardware options, including graphical installation
   instructions.

o  Netscape Navigator -- Provides immediate user access to the Internet.

Multia X Server V3.1 Option for Intel

The Multia X Server V3.1 Option for Intel is a local application that
provides interoperability with UNIX and OpenVMS X applications. This X
server provides performance and features equivalent to best-in-class X
terminals. It is fully integrated into the Configuration Manager so that
all of its features can be remotely customized and managed for workgroups
and individual Multia users. This feature is unique in the market. With
the Multia X Server Option, users can run UNIX and OpenVMS X applications
alongside Windows NT, Windows 95, Windows, and legacy applications. All
these applications can be accessed simultaneously using different network
protocols. Features include

o  Optimized X11.R6 X server
o  Local OSF/Motif Window manager
o  X image extension
o  NFS client software
o  Font support for X Font Server, SNF, BDF, and PCF font formats
o  Font failover
o  Font access via font server, DAP, NFS, and TCP/IP
o  Cut and paste between X windows and Microsoft Windows
o  XDM host chooser
o  Backing store/save under
o  Shape extension

RUMBA for Mainframe for Multia V3.1 for Intel

The RUMBA for Mainframe for Multia V3.1 for Intel option allows Multia
users to interactively access IBM mainframe applications. Connections to
the IBM mainframe can be made via an industry-standard gateway supporting
TN3270 sessions, via a Microsoft SNA server, or via a front-end processor
on a mainframe supporting TN3270 sessions. Other features include

o  Emulation of the following 3270 display stations: 3278/79, 3178/79,
   3179-G, 3192-G, and 3472-G. All popular terminal models (2 through 5) and
   screen sizes are supported.

o  Auto Font Control feature adjusts the character font size automatically
   to fit the window.

o  Truetype font support.

o  Supports the most popular keyboard configurations, which can be selected
   from a menu.

o  QuickStep macro function enables users to assign command and keystroke
   sequences to a single key. Users can also create macros for automating
   functions; for example, opening other Windows applications.

o  Hotspots function activates macros by pointing and clicking the mouse on
   a special text on the screen.

o  Cut and paste data between two applications.

o  Hotlinks enable automatic data exchanges between a Windows and mainframe
   application.

o  Floating toolbar puts the most frequently used commands on the button bar
   that appears at the top of the RUMBA session.

o  Online, context-sensitive help.

Multia System Administrator's Kit V3.1 for Intel

The Multia System Administrator's Kit V3.1 for Intel provides additional
tools for the system administrator. One kit per installation is required.
The kit consists of CD-ROM media and installation instructions and Multia
Software for Systems Administrator's V3.1, which includes the following
software:

o  Multia Base Software V3.1
o  Remote Maintenance Facility for remote restoration of user configurations
o  Windows NT and OpenVMS host kits
o  Required host software for Multia X Server and PCNFS daemon
o  Multia required fonts
o  Configuration templates for creating workgroups
o  Online systems administrator's tutorial
o  Multia X Server, RUMBA for Mainframe software options
o  Hardcopy system administrator's guide
o  Single-user license

BENEFITS

o  Centralized configuration management provides the lowest cost of
   ownership for a desktop device.

o  Highly integrated hardware design offers standard components that are
   optional on today's PCs, but are required for an enterprise desktop.

o  Superior interoperability features include embedded network protocols,
   emulators, and an integrated X server. The result is easier access to
   applications across the enterprise and a smooth migration to Windows NT
   client/server computing.

o  Robust security features protect data and applications.

PRODUCT POSITIONING

The Multia family has a dual-architecture strategy to support the
different requirements of the enterprise client market. Both the Alpha-
and Intel-based Multia systems support the same embedded software and
software options. The Multia Alpha line is primarily for users in
technical markets who need to run floating point applications that take
advantage of the Alpha architecture, such as MCAD, ECAD, software
development, and technical publications. The Multia Intel line addresses
the commercial desktop market where the user environment is typically
made up of replicated workgroups, and where Microsoft Windows and Intel
are standard. Here, the ability to run both 16-bit and 32-bit Windows and
Windows NT applications, along with UNIX, OpenVMS, and terminal
applications, is critical.

Digital's XL family of personal workstations offers a range of products
that are positioned to achieve the best application performance in the
expanding market of Windows NT-based workstations. The Multia Enterprise
Client users who need interoperability and central management, as well as
performance. Over 90 percent of Multia system users are using UNIX or
OpenVMS solutions today, but are steadily migrating toward Windows NT.
These users value the additional embedded software features of Multia.

