Digital's Internet Services Roadmap

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Outlines users' needs for the Internet and Digital's supporting services

o  Systems Integration services help users plan and integrate business
   solutions for the Internet

o  Network services help users establish the network infrastructure required
   for Internet access

o  Outsourcing services are available for users who do not want to manage
   Internet servers inhouse

DESCRIPTION

Digital's Internet strategy, the Internet Services Roadmap, addresses
four basic questions users ask about the Internet and how Digital's
services answer those questions.

o  What can the Internet do for my business?
   - Digital can help with evaluation and planning.

o  How can I connect to the Internet?
   - Digital can help with basic connectivity.

o  How do I conduct business over the Internet?
   - Digital can advise about business usage.

o  How do I support the Internet infrastructure?
   - Digital can put together a manageable Internet operating environment.

Some users do not have Internet connections because of legacy systems,
uncertainty about cost/benefits, or security concerns. For these users,
planning services, specifically Executive Workshops, Internet Business
Planning, and Internet Business Pilots, can be a cost-effective way to
understand the risks and benefits of using the Internet.

Users who want to connect with the Internet can take advantage of
connectivity services, such as Technical Assessment, Firewall , Security
Review, Server and Client Startup, and other network services. Those
users who are already connected to the Internet may be interested in
solving specific business problems, such as reducing costs, increasing
revenues, or improving user satisfaction. Digital offers a number of
application services; Web Information Architecture, Application/Data
Integration, Internet Collaboration, and Electronic Commerce.

Once users have set up an Internet infrastructure and applications, they
may need help operating and managing that infrastructure. Digital's
management services -- Web Server Support, Webmaster Services, Web Server
Management, and Internet Gateway Management -- address those needs.

The Internet Services Roadmap has evolved into all-inclusive services
because Digital played a key role in the development of Internet
technologies and is a leading user of the Internet for business
applications. Digital has established external Web home pages, product
bulletin boards, electronic catalogs, and commercial applications.
Through Digital, users have established secure connections, set-up home
pages, published product information, traded goods and services, and
counted election results.

BENEFITS

o  Service offerings are based on Digital's own experiences with the
   Internet

o  Comprehensive set of services

o  Available as fixed-price packages and customized services

o  Complement to partner offerings

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

All of the services under the Internet Services Roadmap are available now
from Digital.

