TZ88 Digital Linear Tape Drive

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Unprecedented capacity of up to 40 GB per cartridge

o  Read/write compatibility with Tx85, Tx86, and Tx87 formats, allowing for
   application flexibility and investment protection

o  First products in a new family of TZ88-based subsystems

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The TZ88 digital linear tape (DLT) drive extends the DLT family to new
levels of capacity, with up to 40 GB of capacity per cartridge -- two
times the capacity of the TZ87 drive. With this new level of capacity,
high-end workstations, as well as network servers and systems, now have
enhanced unattended backup/restore and archival capabilities. When
combined with the high reliability and industry-leading data integrity of
DLT capabilities, the TZ88 is a true heavy-duty tape drive for
Hierarchical Storage Management (HSM), image/multimedia storage,
archiving, near-online storage, and unattended backup applications.

The TZ88 tape drive provides read/write support for the existing
CompacTape III (10 GB native/20 GB compressed) product, as well as the
new CompacTape IIIXT (15 GB/20 GB compressed), and CompacTapeIV (20 GB
native/40 GB compressed) media. The TZ88 provides full data interchange
capabilities to the Tx85, Tx86, and Tx87 subsystems. The TZ88 is not read
compatible with older tape formats, such as the TZ30, TK50, and TK70
products.

A family of loader products based on the TZ88 will be announced in early
1996.

BENEFITS

o  Unattended capacity -- With up to 40 GB of capacity, the TZ88 sets a new
   price/capacity point for unattended backup for virtually all high-end
   workstations, as well as many servers and systems.

o  High backup performance -- Supports a transfer rate of up to 2.5 MB per
   second and over 9 GB per hour. This rate meets or exceeds the
   requirements of most systems and server installations (actual performance
   varies with system load, applications software, configuration, and other
   system level factors).

o  Restore performance -- Fast search capability ensures quick data access
   for both emergency restore situations, as well as applications such as
   HSM and archiving.

o  Drive reliability -- Advanced linear tape path design maintains a low
   constant tension between the tape and read/write head, minimizing head
   wear and extending the drive's useful life when compared to other
   alternatives.

o  Subsystem reliability -- Digital's extensive device qualification and
   system integration testing ensure that the TZ88 saves and restores
   critical data without compromising data integrity.

o  Investment protection -- Compatibility with Tx85, Tx86, and Tx87 products
   ensures that previously written data can continue to be accessed.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The TZ88 drive can be ordered now from Digital and its business partners.

CompacTape IIIXT and CompacTapeIV media are increasingly available from a
variety of distributors and resellers. Users in the U.S. can purchase
